# ARC-105 signed managed load fixture

Run on ownsolid-cpu as root from this private runner directory. The
launcher never starts work without the explicit run flag and its capacity
check. It checks the host again after staging and checks live cgroups
before releasing the simulator.

```sh
bash launch.sh --check
bash launch.sh --run
```

Exit 75 means resource admission refused the launch. Read `prelaunch.json`
for the recorded host snapshot and reason. The launcher uses the signed
test media and staged KWOK inputs from the prior ARC-only fixtures. It
copies the signed archive and public trust to separate test media after
admission. No release signer is needed.

The run creates its own `run.*` directory and internal Docker network.
It records the exact test process exit, resource admission and samples,
managed API output, the unchanged packet and DNS records, the KWOK
Node and Pod proof, simulator report, database windows and dispatch and
reconnect samples under that directory. Cleanup removes the isolated
containers and per-run node credentials. It leaves evidence and test
media on the host.

The five-second pacing and the one hundred facts tasks per minute are
fixed. Measure ten full one-minute windows after both the gateway fleet
and KWOK workload are ready. The two real RKE2 members stay outside the
1,000 synthetic UUIDs. The process must exit zero to pass.
